KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ member moved: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ move is non-throwing: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The implicit move constructor is declared only when a subobject is
move-only (declare_implicit_move in cpp_typecheck_compound_type.cpp), not
under the conditions of [class.copy.ctor]/8.  Holder(std::move(a)) then
calls the implicit copy constructor, which copies the member, and the
noexcept operator reads the copy constructor's specification.  Both
assertions 1 and 2 fail.
